{"title":"Proper divisor","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>proper divisor</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integer</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisor</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> itself.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has no proper divisors, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_number\" title=\"Prime number\">prime numbers</a> have exactly one proper divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and all other positive integers have at least two proper divisors.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Proper_divisor&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Deficient_number\" title=\"Deficient number\">Deficient number</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Abundant_number\" title=\"Abundant number\">Abundant number</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_number\" title=\"Perfect number\">Perfect number</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Proper_divisor&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013913\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 37/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 855/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.393      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.393      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3967:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018013913 and revision id 153496. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}